# Analysis Methodology

## Approach

The analysis uses a five-year trend-based approach covering FY2020–FY2024.

## Analysis Areas

### Financial Position
Analyses changes in Total Assets and Shareholders' Equity to understand balance-sheet expansion and capital development.

### Financial Performance
Compares Operating Income and Operating Expenses to assess income generation and cost growth.

### Profitability
Analyses Profit After Tax, ROAA and ROAE to evaluate profitability and returns.

### Asset Quality
Uses Gross NPL Ratio and Loan Loss Coverage Ratio to assess credit risk and provisioning strength.

### Liquidity
Uses the Liquidity Ratio to assess liquidity and short-term financial resilience.

## Trend Analysis

Year-on-year movements and FY2020–FY2024 changes are used to identify significant trends and changes in financial performance.

## Business Interpretation

The analysis translates financial trends into management implications and recommendations rather than focusing only on descriptive statistics.

## Data Integrity

Only reported figures are used. Missing financial information is not estimated or fabricated.